1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,276
Welcome to Daily Brief.

2
00:00:02,226 --> 00:00:06,130
It's Saturday, November 28th, 2026.

3
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:08,797
Three stories in about three minutes.

4
00:00:08,797 --> 00:00:13,488
First, a legal fight between two of the most valuable companies on earth.

5
00:00:13,488 --> 00:00:19,750
OpenAI has filed a counterclaim against Apple, accusing it of misappropriating trade secrets.

6
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:27,369
According to foreign media reports, the dispute concerns technology and personnel connected to OpenAI's hardware efforts.

7
00:00:27,369 --> 00:00:36,785
The filing marks a sharp turn: the two companies were partners not long ago, and Apple's AI features were widely expected to lean on OpenAI's models.

8
00:00:36,785 --> 00:00:45,619
Lawsuits between platform owners and model builders are becoming the defining argument of this cycle, and this one has the deepest pockets on both sides.

9
00:00:45,619 --> 00:00:48,523
Second, a tragedy in the Atlantic.

10
00:00:48,523 --> 00:00:57,071
Fourteen people have died and ninety were rescued after a migrant boat was found adrift about seventy two kilometres from Spain's island of El Hierro.

11
00:00:57,071 --> 00:01:00,928
Spanish news agency EFE reported the numbers.

12
00:01:00,928 --> 00:01:08,750
The route to the Canary Islands has become one of the deadliest in the world, and this is the second mass-casualty incident on it this month.

13
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:15,321
Survivors are being processed on the island, where reception capacity has been under strain for over a year.

14
00:01:15,321 --> 00:01:18,654
Third, diplomacy with a guest list attached.

15
00:01:18,654 --> 00:01:25,178
President Trump said President Putin would be welcome at the G20, telling reporters he would like him to attend.

16
00:01:25,178 --> 00:01:31,047
The remark comes days after Trump publicly urged Putin to end military aggression in Europe.

17
00:01:31,047 --> 00:01:36,559
Whether Russia would accept is unclear, and no formal invitation has been described.

18
00:01:36,559 --> 00:01:41,857
But the signal matters: Washington is reopening a channel it spent two years closing.

19
00:01:41,857 --> 00:01:44,083
That's your briefing for today.

20
00:01:44,083 --> 00:01:46,940
The full transcript is in the show notes.

21
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,000
I'll be back on Monday.

